---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import Address from '../components/Address.astro'
import { PAGES } from '../data/pages'
import { COMPANY, PRO, inr, taxNote } from '../data/company'

const monthly = inr(PRO.monthlyInr)
const yearly = inr(PRO.yearlyInr)
---

<Legal
  page={PAGES.terms}
  h1="Terms of service"
  intro="These terms cover the Ferrocast app, this website and the optional Ferrocast Pro subscription. They are written to be read, not skimmed past."
>
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    Ferrocast is made by {COMPANY.legalName} (“{COMPANY.name}”, “we”), a {COMPANY.entityType} of {COMPANY.proprietor} based in {COMPANY.address.city}, {COMPANY.address.region}, India, registered as an MSME under Udyam number {COMPANY.udyam}. You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> or through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The app is free software</h2>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    The Ferrocast desktop app, its dashboard and overlays are released under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html" rel="noopener">GNU General Public License, version 3</a>. The licence, not these terms, decides what you may do with the code: use it for any purpose, study it, change it and share it under the same licence. Nothing here limits those rights.
  </p>
  <p>
    “Ferrocast” and the Ferrocast logo are trademarks of {COMPANY.name}. If you share a modified
    version, give it a different name so people can tell it apart from ours.
  </p>

  <h2>Using Ferrocast with streaming platforms</h2>
  <p>
    Ferrocast connects to Twitch, YouTube and Kick with the permissions you approve. You stay
    responsible for following each platform’s rules, and for what your bot, alerts and overlays
    show. We are not affiliated with any platform, and a platform may change or end its service in
    ways that affect Ferrocast.
  </p>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    If you connect YouTube, you also agree to be bound by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, because Ferrocast uses YouTube API Services. Our <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains what that means for your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips</h2>
  <p>
    When you set up a tip page, viewers pay through your own account with a payment provider such as
    Razorpay, Stripe or Ko-fi. The payment is between the viewer, you and that provider. We never
    hold, receive or pass on the money and take no cut. Refunds and disputes for tips are handled by
    you and your provider under the provider’s terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Ferrocast Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is an optional subscription for services we run on our servers, bought in the app under
    Settings › Pro:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Prices are in Indian rupees ({monthly} a month or {yearly} a year at launch). {taxNote()}
      Payments are processed by Razorpay, which also sends your payment receipt. Other currencies
      are shown only as an estimate.
    </li>
    <li>
      You must be 18 or over to buy Pro, or have the consent of a parent or lawful guardian who
      agrees to these terms for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      Subscriptions renew automatically until you cancel. See
      <a href="/refunds/#auto-renew">how renewal works and how to cancel</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      If we change the price, we will tell you at least 60 days before it applies to you, and you
      keep your price for at least 12 months from the start of your subscription.
    </li>
    <li>
      We will never move a free feature into Pro, and never remove a feature from a plan you pay
      for, except as described under <a href="#closing">If we close a cloud service</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Refunds follow our <a href="/refunds/">refund and cancellation policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="pro-services">What Pro includes</h2>
  <p>Pro covers these services. Each one runs on our servers.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>24/7 cloud bot.</strong> Your commands, timers and auto-replies keep running on Twitch
      and Kick when your PC is off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dashboard from anywhere.</strong> Your dashboard on your phone, for you and the mods
      you invite. Offline mode: with the cloud bot on, chat, bans and history keep working when your
      PC is off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ferrocast voices.</strong> Text-to-speech voices made by Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord bot.</strong> Go-live posts in your server and roles for your supporters.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloud backups.</strong> Encrypted copies of your setup, locked on your PC before
      upload.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream history.</strong> Totals for every stream.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Weekly email.</strong> An optional report of your week’s streams.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tip branding and goal.</strong> Your colours and images on the tip page, and a tip
      goal.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A YouTube cloud bot and custom tip addresses are coming later. They are not part of Pro until
    they ship.
  </p>
  <p>
    One subscription covers up to 3 of your PCs. Pro never posts to your audience on its own and
    never puts our name on your overlays or tip page. The cloud bot sends only what you set up, and
    you are responsible for it, as with the bot on your PC.
  </p>

  <h2 id="fair-use">Fair-use limits</h2>
  <p>
    Pro has limits so it stays fast and affordable for everyone. They apply per subscription unless
    we say otherwise. When you reach one, the app tells you which limit it was and when it resets.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloud bot:</strong> one channel per platform, up to 20 messages a minute per channel,
      50 timers, 500 commands and 256 KB of bot settings.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dashboard from anywhere:</strong> up to 5 of your own devices and 10 mods per PC, and
      up to 20 requests a second per device.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ferrocast voices:</strong> 20,000 characters a month and up to 300 characters a line.
      If the voices across all of Pro reach their shared monthly limit, they rest until the 1st and
      your app reads with your system voice instead.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord bot:</strong> one server, 10 role rules and 5,000 linked viewers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloud backups:</strong> 250 MB and 7 backups in total, and up to 6 uploads a day. The
      oldest automatic backup makes room for a new one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream history:</strong> up to 400 days. The weekly email goes only in weeks you
      streamed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tip page:</strong> 30 image uploads a day.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Streaming platforms set their own limits too. Ferrocast tells you when a platform refuses or
    limits an action.
  </p>

  <h2 id="lapse">When Pro ends</h2>
  <p>
    Pro ends when you cancel and the paid period runs out, when every renewal attempt fails, or when
    a payment is refunded.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Cloud work stops at our next hourly check. The free app keeps working as before.</li>
    <li>
      We keep your Pro data for 30 days. During that time you can still download your cloud backups
      and your stream history.
    </li>
    <li>
      Roles the Ferrocast bot gave in your Discord server are removed when Pro ends. The bot leaves
      your server after the 30 days.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you buy Pro again within the 30 days, you keep everything: your stream history, backups,
      cloud bot, Discord setup and weekly email move to the new subscription.
    </li>
    <li>
      After that, we delete the data, as described in the
      <a href="/privacy/#pro-data">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is a digital service, provided from India. It is activated on your Ferrocast account right
    after a successful payment, and you get a receipt by email. Nothing is shipped.
  </p>

  <h2 id="closing">If we close a cloud service</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever shut down a service that runs on our servers, we will give at least 180 days’ notice,
    keep export available until the end, and refund any unused prepaid time.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We will tell you by email, on this website and in the app’s release notes, at least 180 days
      before the service stops.
    </li>
    <li>
      Until the last day, you can download what that service keeps for you: your cloud backups, your
      stream history as a spreadsheet file, and your bot settings, which also stay in the app on
      your PC.
    </li>
    <li>
      Unused prepaid time is refunded without you having to ask, as the
      <a href="/refunds/">refund policy</a> says.
    </li>
    <li>The app and the relay are open source under GPL-3.0, so anyone can keep running them.</li>
    <li>Everything that runs on your PC keeps working. Free stays free.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This promise covers every Pro service, including ones we add later.</p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Do not use Ferrocast’s hosted services (the relay, tip pages and Pro) to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law, or the rules of the platforms you stream on;</li>
    <li>harass, threaten or dox anyone, or run hate raids;</li>
    <li>attack, overload or try to get around the security of our servers;</li>
    <li>collect money for anything illegal or for goods you do not deliver.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We may suspend hosted services for an account that does, and will tell you why when we can.</p>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>
    The hosted services are for people aged 18 or over. If you are under 18, you may use them only
    with the consent of a parent or lawful guardian, who agrees to these terms for you.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The app is provided as is, as the GPL-3.0 says. We work hard to keep it reliable, but we cannot
    promise it will be free of bugs or that platforms will keep their APIs working. Keep your own
    exports and backups.
  </p>

  <h2>Limit of liability</h2>
  <p>
    As far as the law allows, we are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost
    revenue from a stream. For Pro, our total liability is limited to what you paid us in the 12
    months before the claim. Nothing here limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be
    limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    If we change these terms in a way that matters, we will update the date above and, for Pro
    subscribers, email you at least 30 days before the change applies.
  </p>

  <h2 id="grievance">Complaints and grievance officer</h2>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    If something is wrong, write to our grievance officer, {COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.name}, at <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}`}>{COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}</a> or call {COMPANY.phone}. We acknowledge every complaint within {COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.ackHours} hours and resolve it within one month of receiving it.
  </p>

  <h2>Law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of India. Disputes go to {COMPANY.jurisdiction}. Before
    that, please write to us; most problems are solved by talking. This does not take away your
    right to go to a consumer commission under the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <Address />
  <p>
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a>
  </p>
</Legal>
